# ================================================================
#  This artifact operates under the same principle as the engine
#  itself: what appears as noise to the untrained eye carries
#  structure to those who know where to look.
#
#  The blockchain does not hide its secrets behind encryption.
#  It hides them behind complexity — just like this.
#
#  CIPRIAN STEFAN PLESCA — independent researcher, Romania, 2025
#  "Entropy is not randomness. It is order waiting to be decoded."
# ================================================================

# ── INSTRUCTION SET ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   jmp (D)          →  trace the fund flow
#   out A            →  surface the anomaly
#   in  A            →  ingest raw transaction graph
#   rotr(D); A=(D)   →  rotate the cluster heuristic
#   mov D,(D)        →  traverse the peeling chain
#   nop              →  clean address — pass through
#   halt             →  cashout detected. stop.
#   A=(D) op A       →  apply CIOH — merge inputs into cluster
#
# ── REGISTER MAP ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   A  →  risk_score       (accumulator)
#   C  →  tx_pointer       (code pointer — self-modifying)
#   D  →  address_cursor   (data pointer)
#
# ── MEMORY ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   59,049 ternary cells — one for each address in the graph.
#   Each cell transforms after execution.
#   Like every address touched by a mixer: it is never the same
#   twice.
#
# ── PATTERN SIGNATURES ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   PEELING CHAIN      ::  C advances linearly, D follows offset
#   FAN-OUT            ::  single A forks across D[0..n]
#   FAN-IN             ::  D[0..n] converges — A accumulates
#   RAPID PASS-THROUGH ::  jmp fires before out — no dwell time
#   CASHOUT NODE       ::  halt — terminal. risk_score = MAX.
#
# ── CRAZY OPERATION (op) — the one table no blockchain uses ──────
#
#          A
#          0    1    2
#   D  0 [ 1    0    0 ]
#      1 [ 1    0    2 ]
#      2 [ 2    2    1 ]
#
#   Three inputs. Nine outputs. Irreversible.
#   The on-chain equivalent: CoinJoin.
#
# ── EXECUTION NOTE ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   This program was not written by a human.
#   Neither was the transaction graph it models.
#
#   Both required a machine to produce.
#   Both require a human to interpret.
#   That gap — is exactly what ofi-chain-forensics fills.
#
